Apple has suffered a yo-yo-effect.
It's all for the displays.
A more powerful-than-redefinition-retale-retroversial processor, a stronger chassis or a touch-enabled display, these are, in short, the advantages of the Nin-season’s recently introduced iPhone.
The last two then also have a negative impact on the dimensions and weights of iPhones 6s and 6s Plus.
Apple's trend so far has been that every new generation of the iPhone is lighter than the previous one.
An exception was only the third and fourth-generation, the weight of which increased slightly compared to the previous iPhones.
A two-greater weight difference to the detriment of the news was really negligible.
However, this is far from the case with new iPhones.
Compared to last year's iPhone 6 and 6 Plus, the weight has increased by 14 grams for a smaller model, with 20 grams larger.
On the one hand, it is not astonishing, last year's bending affair was greatly tormented by bending in Apple's pockets.
The propeoche of novelties is thus made of a more resufficient aluminum alloy 7000, which was also projected on the weight.
However, the displays have a much bigger impact on it.
Apple has used 3D Touch technology for the novelty, thanks to which the displays recognize the power of touch.
To do this, it was necessary to provide the display with an additional stratum of capacitive sensors.
Thus, the weight of new iPhone displays increased more than twice as much compared to previous generations.
For a smaller iPhone originally from 12 grams to 29 grams, in the case of a larger then from 19 to 40 grams.
For an iphone 6s, the display is the heaviest-guide used component.
The weight of only 143 grams is then achieved in this novelty thanks to the slimming corce, which has affected most of the remaining components.
For a larger model, the heaviest element of the battery is used, but its weight did not change compared to its predecessor.
Even in this case, the biggest increase is noticeable for the display.
The 5.5-inch iPhone 6s Plus weight thus reaches 192 grams.
The extent to which the new technology of the display will be practical will manifest itself only when it comes to use.
The first users will be able to try it as early as Friday, September 25, when the sale of iPhone 6s and 6s Plus will be launched in selected countries.
