The symbol of the municipality came to life.
The wheel of the windmill above Chlum is rotating again after many years.
It can be seen far away because it is placed on a fifteen-metre-high mast.
People from a wide entourage call it a "terrifier on Chlum".
For the municipality with 150 inhabitants it even became one of the elements of the communal emblem, which the municipality gained on the occasion of a meeting of natives in 2010.
"At that time we applied for the emblem and, of course, we wanted to have the fan on the emblem, everyone knows it in the area," Mayor Jiří Mašek said.
Chlum wind pump is a local technical monument.
It is a bit of a memento of the present: it is reminiscent of a time when local people struggled for high-quality drinking water.
It was a rarity in Chlum in the past centuries.
It wasn’t until 1910 that Chlum councillors opted for a solution, which then met until the mid-1980s.
In the municipality at the turn-branch on Číchov, they were excavated a seven-metre-seated well.
Three-year-old years later the well was supplemented by a metal structure with a wind pump, which pumped the water into the reservoir at the highest point of the village, near the local church.
"Building was carried out by Antonín Kunc from Hranice na Moravě with a cost of 2 400 crowns," says the commemorative inscribation on the ground-floor fencing of the mast structure.
The pump was retired after several repairs and crashes of the wind wheel in 1971.
On May 7,, 1973, a new chapter began to be the beginning of the fight for water: a new water supply began to serve that day in Chlum.
The wind pump remained only a non-functional communal symbol and local rarity.
They put the dominatrix at this year's retirement.
It wasn't until 2008 that Chlumsky decided to repair the windy bike again and rectify it again.
They made a replica of the original wheel - scaled in diameter by half a metre.
The bike was fitted on a mast, but it still had to be brought down that same year.
Replica manufacturer did not choose a suitable material, and the bike could not defy gneiders of the gneiders of the wind.
Then for a few years the chlum's domicile rest disassembled under the roof.
Since June this year, however, the bike on a high mast has been rotating again.
On the occasion of the retirement of the natives, the municipality had a replica modified and reassembled it to the top of the iron tower.
But the bike draws the service water from the well only into the amblining blind shoulder.
And during the summer we completely disconnected it, because there was not enough water in the well.
It was at least fussy.
"In the autumn we will reconcile the wind wheel shaft from the pump in the suction basket," the mayor of Masek explained.
Chlum is not the only municipality in the Czech Republic, where a windy bike has reached the municipal emblem, however, it is the only village of this species in the whole Vysočina region.
They have a similar element in the emblacim in honor of local technical monuments, for example in Chvalkovice and Zelená Hora in the Vyškov region, Kuželov in the Hodonín region, Partutovice in the Přerov region or in Police in the Vsetín region.
