Kofola is moving from Poland to the Czech Republic and is considering entering the Prague Stock Exchange.
Kofola should have a new headquarters in Ostrava.
Kofola S.A. was registered in Poland due to the trading of the company's shares on the Warsaw Stock Exchange.
Our primary goal is to have a group headquarters in the Czech Republic.
The steps we have taken so far within the scope of the project are mainly legal and administrative and do not have a de facto impact on what is happening in the company, says Daniel Buryš, Chief Financial Officer of the Kofola Group.
"In connection with the transfer of the group's headquarters, shareholders are considering the placement of shares on the Prague Stock Exchange."
Due to its accession to the Prague Stock Exchange, the company is finalizing the prospectus of the security, which it will present to the Czech National Bank for approval in the near future.
Moving the registered office of the holding and related transfers of shares will be carried out in the form of a non-prepayable transaction, with only existing shareholders.
As part of this operation, therefore, there will be no equivalretion shares to the public or to new investors.
"A possible offer of shares to new investors would take place - if the company and its shareholders so decide - at a later date, either in the 4th quarter of 2015 or in the first quarter of 2016," the company said.
The company has said in the past that an eventual offer of shares could consist of the issuance of new shares or the sale of existing shares.
This offer could consist of an offer of equities on the stock exchange in the Czech Republic and in Poland, including the placement of shares also on the Warsaw Stock Exchange.
